  "reason": "The exact pinned candidate forms one continuous low limestone and flowstone face along the declared N upper-right diagonal, with layered calcite, small stalagmites, and pale rubble consistent with the cave reference. It remains continuous and readable at runtime scale, stays a narrow height-1 boundary rather than a terrain tile, and shows no concrete orientation, seam, category, or generation defect. Normalization is current and detects only the N ground band. Coverage is 64 per mille with 128x96 bounds and transparent corners; the ground envelope remains within 0.2 pixels of the N segment across all thirds and reaches the endpoints within 3 pixels and 10 pixels.",
